Atonota changes to cloudflightio/keycloak-magic-link

Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflightio/keycloak-magic-link
Pinned commit: 7b4ee949a39a7ee953987162479ae1da2c57c3cb
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (the upstream LICENSE file).

The image build unpacks the pinned upstream archive and copies the files in
this folder over it. All other files come unchanged from the upstream archive.

Changed on 24 November 2026 for G-162 (design: backend/docs/decisions/0003-keycloak-extensions.md):

- Modified: src/main/java/io/cloudflight/keycloak/magiclink/authenticators/AbstractMagicLinkAuthenticator.java
  The request does the same work for an existing and an unknown address.
  The link row and the mail are written by a background job after the request.
  The mail is sent only within the per-address send limit.
  A failed mail is logged without the link and no longer answers with HTTP 500.
- Modified: src/main/java/io/cloudflight/keycloak/magiclink/authenticators/AbstractMagicLinkAuthenticatorFactory.java
  Declares the two send limit settings, so the admin API shows them unmasked.
- Added: src/main/java/io/cloudflight/keycloak/magiclink/sending/MagicLinkSendLimiter.java
  Counts sent mails per address in Keycloak's single use object store.
  Settings: magiclink.send.limit (default 3) and magiclink.send.window.seconds (default 900).
